# region Invoke-NSUnsetSSLCrl
function Invoke-NSUnsetSSLCrl {
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
        Clears one or more NetScaler sslcrl resource properties.
    .DESCRIPTION
        Configuration for Certificate Revocation List resource.
    .PARAMETER CrlName
        Name for the Certificate Revocation List (CRL). Must begin with an ASCII alphanumeric or underscore (_) character, and must contain only ASCII alphanumeric, underscore, hash (#), period (.), space, colon (:), at (@), equals (=), and hyphen (-) characters. Cannot be changed after the CRL is created. The following requirement applies only to the Citrix ADC CLI: If the name includes one or more spaces, enclose the name in double or single quotation marks (for example, "my crl" or 'my crl'). Minimum length = 1
    .PARAMETER Basedn
        Base distinguished name (DN), which is used in an LDAP search to search for a CRL. Citrix recommends searching for the Base DN instead of the Issuer Name from the CA certificate, because the Issuer Name field might not exactly match the LDAP directory structure's DN. Minimum length = 1
    .PARAMETER Binary
        Set the LDAP-based CRL retrieval mode to binary. Default value: NO Possible values = YES, NO
    .PARAMETER Binddn
        Bind distinguished name (DN) to be used to access the CRL object in the LDAP repository if access to the LDAP repository is restricted or anonymous access is not allowed. Minimum length = 1
    .PARAMETER CaCert
        CA certificate that has issued the CRL. Required if CRL Auto Refresh is selected. Install the CA certificate on the appliance before adding the CRL. Minimum length = 1
    .PARAMETER Day
        Day on which to refresh the CRL, or, if the Interval parameter is not set, the number of days after which to refresh the CRL. If Interval is set to MONTHLY, specify the date. If Interval is set to WEEKLY, specify the day of the week (for example, Sun=0 and Sat=6). This parameter is not applicable if the Interval is set to DAILY. Minimum value = 0 Maximum value = 31
    .PARAMETER Interval
        CRL refresh interval. Use the NONE setting to unset this parameter. Possible values = MONTHLY, WEEKLY, DAILY, NOW, NONE
    .PARAMETER Method
        Method for CRL refresh. If LDAP is selected, specify the method, CA certificate, base DN, port, and LDAP server name. If HTTP is selected, specify the CA certificate, method, URL, and port. Cannot be changed after a CRL is added. Possible values = HTTP, LDAP
    .PARAMETER Password
        Password to access the CRL in the LDAP repository if access to the LDAP repository is restricted or anonymous access is not allowed. Minimum length = 1
    .PARAMETER Port
        Port for the LDAP server. Minimum value = 1
    .PARAMETER Refresh
        Set CRL auto refresh. Possible values = ENABLED, DISABLED
    .PARAMETER Scope
        Extent of the search operation on the LDAP server. Available settings function as follows: One - One level below Base DN. Base - Exactly the same level as Base DN. Default value: One Possible values = Base, One
    .PARAMETER Server
        IP address of the LDAP server from which to fetch the CRLs. Minimum length = 1
    .PARAMETER Time
        Time, in hours (1-24) and minutes (1-60), at which to refresh the CRL.
    .PARAMETER URL
        URL of the CRL distribution point.
    .PARAMETER Session
